So I had Claude do a bit of digging and it looks like an issue with the way that Experimental async is interacting with bits-ui.

Fixable in bits-ui but not completely sure if it would be something better raised to Svelte itself. Either way probably good to just fix it.

Looks like the fix is to watch `.current` instead of `afterTick` here.
```diff
--- a/packages/bits-ui/src/lib/internal/animations-complete.ts
+++ b/packages/bits-ui/src/lib/internal/animations-complete.ts
@@ -114,11 +114,11 @@
 	#executeCallback(fn: () => void | Promise<void>): void {
 		const execute = () => {
 			fn();
 		};

-		if (this.#opts.afterTick) {
+		if (this.#opts.afterTick.current) {
 			afterTick(execute);
 		} else {
 			execute();
 		}
 	}
 }
```

You can patch this in bits-ui as a workaround until a fix is merged.
